WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.950
- The last time you were here,
so we weren't able to hug.

00:00:02.950 --> 00:00:04.847
- No I got so excited to touch you.

00:00:05.920 --> 00:00:07.030
- I know, the embrace was nice.

00:00:07.030 --> 00:00:10.650
So, and our lives were very
different, both of them,

00:00:10.650 --> 00:00:12.190
God, a lot has happened.
- Yes!

00:00:12.190 --> 00:00:14.100
We should go out for a drink after this.

00:00:14.100 --> 00:00:16.440
- I don't know if that'd be good.

00:00:16.440 --> 00:00:17.273
We can go out for a drink right now.

00:00:17.273 --> 00:00:18.380
Justin, here we go.

00:00:18.380 --> 00:00:20.057
Yeah!
- Oh my gosh!

00:00:20.057 --> 00:00:21.350
- We're gonna go for a drink right now.

00:00:21.350 --> 00:00:23.840
Here's the thing,
- Thank you.

00:00:23.840 --> 00:00:26.305
- It's been a rough go man.
- Thank you!

00:00:26.305 --> 00:00:27.138
- It's been a rough go.
- This is the best thing.

00:00:27.138 --> 00:00:28.090
I didn't expect this.

00:00:28.090 --> 00:00:31.350
- I just wanted to say, I feel you girl.

00:00:31.350 --> 00:00:32.700
- Cheers to us.

00:00:32.700 --> 00:00:35.130
- I'm just saying it's been
a, it's been a rough go.

00:00:35.130 --> 00:00:36.690
- This just became the
most fun talk show ever.

00:00:36.690 --> 00:00:38.980
- But then also you, you were
on the cover of "Glamour."

00:00:38.980 --> 00:00:40.200
- Yes!
- This is amazing.

00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:41.616
Look at this.
- Yeah, thank you.

00:00:41.616 --> 00:00:44.050
(audience cheers)

00:00:44.050 --> 00:00:45.560
Me and my two friends.

00:00:45.560 --> 00:00:47.260
- You are like, first of all.

00:00:47.260 --> 00:00:48.780
Yes ma'am you work hard for that.

00:00:48.780 --> 00:00:50.070
I'd show all that too.

00:00:50.070 --> 00:00:51.420
No, you look so beautiful.

00:00:51.420 --> 00:00:52.780
- Thank you.

00:00:52.780 --> 00:00:53.613
- But you know what it
is, you look beautiful

00:00:53.613 --> 00:00:54.446
but you look really strong.

00:00:54.446 --> 00:00:55.507
- Thank you.
- I love that.

00:00:55.507 --> 00:00:57.480
- I love that "Glamour" does represent

00:00:57.480 --> 00:01:00.420
a lot of like strong women
and just amazing stories.

00:01:00.420 --> 00:01:02.180
And I was so proud to be on the cover.

00:01:02.180 --> 00:01:03.070
And I like it too.

00:01:03.070 --> 00:01:04.350
It feels very fierce.

00:01:04.350 --> 00:01:05.210
- Yeah. I know.

00:01:05.210 --> 00:01:06.043
That was the word.

00:01:06.043 --> 00:01:07.343
What did, so in the article

00:01:07.343 --> 00:01:09.960
you got pretty personal
and very vulnerable.

00:01:09.960 --> 00:01:11.510
That can be hard in this industry.

00:01:11.510 --> 00:01:15.100
- I think for so many years
I have been, I'm very open.

00:01:15.100 --> 00:01:15.933
- Me too.
- Yes you are.

00:01:15.933 --> 00:01:17.750
And that's what I love about you.

00:01:17.750 --> 00:01:20.320
And I'm very happy and life
is normally pretty good.

00:01:20.320 --> 00:01:21.420
And I don't like complaining

00:01:21.420 --> 00:01:23.542
because I have so much to be grateful for.

00:01:23.542 --> 00:01:27.350
And this year I wanted to be very upfront

00:01:27.350 --> 00:01:29.440
that it wasn't my best year.

00:01:29.440 --> 00:01:30.543
- Yeah.

00:01:30.543 --> 00:01:32.348
- And I've been very sad. (laughs)

00:01:32.348 --> 00:01:33.181
- Yeah.

00:01:33.181 --> 00:01:34.410
- I think social media is so wonderful

00:01:34.410 --> 00:01:35.670
for so many reasons.

00:01:35.670 --> 00:01:37.900
But it shows just all the good stuff.

00:01:37.900 --> 00:01:39.434
- All the filtered version of your life.

00:01:39.434 --> 00:01:41.160
- It does, and it makes
you feel kind of crappy

00:01:41.160 --> 00:01:42.380
when you look at someone else's life,

00:01:42.380 --> 00:01:43.750
and you think they have it all.

00:01:43.750 --> 00:01:44.868
- Yeah.

00:01:44.868 --> 00:01:46.420
- And I just wanted to
tell everyone this time

00:01:46.420 --> 00:01:48.210
that not everything is what it seems.

00:01:48.210 --> 00:01:49.770
And I struggle like everybody else

00:01:49.770 --> 00:01:52.530
because I do feel like I put
on a really pretty picture.

00:01:52.530 --> 00:01:55.760
And I just wanted to be
honest, without whining.

00:01:55.760 --> 00:01:57.410
There's like a fine line right?

00:01:57.410 --> 00:01:58.900
- Yes but there's not...

00:01:58.900 --> 00:02:01.010
Yes, but I think that we
are similar in the sense

00:02:01.010 --> 00:02:02.660
that people always assume,
like you're very bubbly.

00:02:02.660 --> 00:02:04.170
you're very nice, you're very welcoming.

00:02:04.170 --> 00:02:05.003
You know what I'm saying?

00:02:05.003 --> 00:02:06.090
Like when we go, people are generally,

00:02:06.090 --> 00:02:09.040
but sometimes our lives aren't great.

00:02:09.040 --> 00:02:10.690
- Yes.
- And sometimes you're sad.

00:02:10.690 --> 00:02:11.523
- Yes.
- And sometimes you don't...

00:02:11.523 --> 00:02:13.540
You know, it's like everybody
expects the comedian

00:02:13.540 --> 00:02:15.344
you know you have to make
people laugh all the time.

00:02:15.344 --> 00:02:16.177
That kind of thing.

00:02:16.177 --> 00:02:17.050
I feel like if you're bubbly

00:02:17.050 --> 00:02:19.930
and like that's our general
personality and we're talkative.

00:02:19.930 --> 00:02:21.400
Like people expect that, and if you're not

00:02:21.400 --> 00:02:22.627
then there's something really wrong.

00:02:22.627 --> 00:02:23.957
And it's like, I'm just having...

00:02:23.957 --> 00:02:24.870
- It's just a normal person.

00:02:24.870 --> 00:02:27.640
- Yes, just a normal person
experiencing emotions.

00:02:27.640 --> 00:02:28.890
- Having a lot going on.

00:02:28.890 --> 00:02:30.940
It's funny too, when I
did open up a little bit

00:02:30.940 --> 00:02:32.690
over the past year, even
with my close friends

00:02:32.690 --> 00:02:34.170
who didn't know much that was going on,

00:02:34.170 --> 00:02:36.000
I kept, I keep a lot of stuff close.

00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:37.010
- Me too.
- Yeah.

00:02:37.010 --> 00:02:39.210
And so they, I found to be so,

00:02:39.210 --> 00:02:41.430
people really wanted to be there for me.

00:02:41.430 --> 00:02:42.630
Like I didn't realize it.

00:02:42.630 --> 00:02:44.300
Like I felt like it was such a burden

00:02:44.300 --> 00:02:46.220
And I was trying to take
on everything by myself

00:02:46.220 --> 00:02:47.550
until I realized I actually physically

00:02:47.550 --> 00:02:48.700
couldn't do it anymore.

00:02:48.700 --> 00:02:50.480
I was actually getting,
making myself sick.

00:02:50.480 --> 00:02:51.510
- Yeah.

00:02:51.510 --> 00:02:52.343
- And I finally like said it out loud,

00:02:52.343 --> 00:02:53.420
like "I need help."

00:02:53.420 --> 00:02:55.730
And saying those words almost killed me.

00:02:55.730 --> 00:02:57.600
And then everyone was
like, "We wanna help you!"

00:02:57.600 --> 00:02:59.530
Like all my friends
came out of the woodwork

00:02:59.530 --> 00:03:00.480
and people at work.

00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:01.313
- Yeah.

00:03:01.313 --> 00:03:02.750
- And I like released
myself from this prison.

00:03:02.750 --> 00:03:04.930
I feel like it was my
own self prison in a way.

00:03:04.930 --> 00:03:07.577
- It's a very vulnerable
place to be there.

00:03:07.577 --> 00:03:09.640
- There've been a lot of tears.

00:03:09.640 --> 00:03:11.983
- I'm loving this too. (Laughs)

00:03:11.983 --> 00:03:13.933
- Okay. Hold on.

00:03:13.933 --> 00:03:17.637
(audience applauds)

00:03:17.637 --> 00:03:18.750
- So you said something else,

00:03:18.750 --> 00:03:19.820
I literally read this article

00:03:19.820 --> 00:03:21.850
and I was like, "Oh my
God, you're in my head."

00:03:21.850 --> 00:03:22.683
- Really?

00:03:22.683 --> 00:03:24.820
- Because you said you'll
never get married again.

00:03:24.820 --> 00:03:26.130
I will never get married again.

00:03:26.130 --> 00:03:27.740
Not because I don't believe in love.

00:03:27.740 --> 00:03:30.175
- I know! Same! I believe in love!

00:03:30.175 --> 00:03:31.710
- Love is beautiful and it's not that.

00:03:31.710 --> 00:03:35.080
I just did mot, that did not suit me.

00:03:35.080 --> 00:03:37.060
- Yeah.
- And yeah, in my life.

00:03:37.060 --> 00:03:40.240
And so I thought it was awesome
that you addressed that.

00:03:40.240 --> 00:03:41.260
Not many people address it,

00:03:41.260 --> 00:03:42.450
'cause I feel like where I'm from

00:03:42.450 --> 00:03:44.000
you have to like, there's steps

00:03:44.000 --> 00:03:46.020
and you have to, and it's just exhausting.

00:03:46.020 --> 00:03:48.210
Cause it doesn't work in
everyone's life like that.

00:03:48.210 --> 00:03:50.340
- Not in this and not the way we work.

00:03:50.340 --> 00:03:53.130
I feel like we're just a
different type of person.

00:03:53.130 --> 00:03:54.960
I want a relationship.
- Me too!

00:03:54.960 --> 00:03:56.650
- Can't wait to have a
partner that I adore.

00:03:56.650 --> 00:03:58.230
And I hope that's there for me.

00:03:58.230 --> 00:04:00.560
But as far as, I don't
know the marriage thing,

00:04:00.560 --> 00:04:02.320
Apparently I'm not great at

00:04:03.250 --> 00:04:05.490
you know, and I'm
accepting my shortcomings.

00:04:05.490 --> 00:04:07.240
- It's a hard thing to do.
- Yes.

00:04:07.240 --> 00:04:08.870
- Especially 'cause a
lot of us get together.

00:04:08.870 --> 00:04:10.140
Like I don't know about y'all,

00:04:10.140 --> 00:04:12.097
but like from where I'm from, once again,

00:04:12.097 --> 00:04:15.250
and I am like, I was old
at 30 to even meet someone

00:04:15.250 --> 00:04:16.340
and then get married at 31.

00:04:16.340 --> 00:04:17.173
That was like old.

00:04:17.173 --> 00:04:19.350
I was almost dead where I'm from.

00:04:19.350 --> 00:04:21.510
Like you know girls are gonna
get married at 20, you know?

00:04:21.510 --> 00:04:22.670
- That is scary.

00:04:22.670 --> 00:04:24.850
- I think, but once you
develop those patterns

00:04:24.850 --> 00:04:27.130
in your life and it's worked,

00:04:27.130 --> 00:04:29.510
it's hard to include another person.

00:04:29.510 --> 00:04:30.453
I'm like 40 years old.

00:04:30.453 --> 00:04:31.286
- It's hard.

00:04:31.286 --> 00:04:32.990
- It's like hard like to do that.

00:04:32.990 --> 00:04:34.527
So anyway, I thought it was awesome.

00:04:34.527 --> 00:04:35.450
- And we love our jobs so much too.

00:04:35.450 --> 00:04:36.283
- I love my job.

00:04:36.283 --> 00:04:37.840
- I talked a lot about
that in the article too.

00:04:37.840 --> 00:04:39.700
Like I'm trying to find some balance now,

00:04:39.700 --> 00:04:40.970
which I feel like I never did,

00:04:40.970 --> 00:04:42.960
it was like one track mind, work, career.

00:04:42.960 --> 00:04:45.450
I know I'm learning to find
the, I think I said it.

00:04:45.450 --> 00:04:47.080
I'm learning to find the gray.

00:04:47.080 --> 00:04:48.280
I'm very black and white.

00:04:48.280 --> 00:04:50.110
My personality is black and white.

00:04:50.110 --> 00:04:52.862
How I go about things and I'm
trying to find some balance

00:04:52.862 --> 00:04:54.610
'cause I've never had that before.

00:04:54.610 --> 00:04:56.200
- I don't know if we
should be real good friends

00:04:56.200 --> 00:04:57.690
'cause I don't think we'd
be good for each other.

00:04:57.690 --> 00:04:59.398
- 'Cause we are exactly the same.

00:04:59.398 --> 00:05:00.930
Am I speaking your language right now?

00:05:00.930 --> 00:05:02.674
- That is so hard for me.

00:05:02.674 --> 00:05:03.507
- It is hard.

00:05:03.507 --> 00:05:04.810
- No it's either in or
out, or it's this or that.

00:05:04.810 --> 00:05:06.170
And it's very hard for me

00:05:06.170 --> 00:05:07.538
'cause then I feel like
I'm just being apathetic

00:05:07.538 --> 00:05:08.776
in the middle.

00:05:08.776 --> 00:05:09.609
- Me too.

00:05:09.609 --> 00:05:10.442
And I don't like the middle road.

00:05:10.442 --> 00:05:11.369
- Me either.
- I'm like one or the other.

00:05:11.369 --> 00:05:12.973
But I have to I have to balance it now.

00:05:12.973 --> 00:05:14.320
- It's healthy. It's healthy.

00:05:14.320 --> 00:05:15.153
No I did too.

00:05:15.153 --> 00:05:16.600
I started saying, "No," a lot.

00:05:16.600 --> 00:05:18.730
So one of your friends and costars

00:05:18.730 --> 00:05:19.563
on "The Flight Attendant,"

00:05:19.563 --> 00:05:20.690
I love "The Flight Attendant,"
- Thank you!

00:05:20.690 --> 00:05:22.800
- I'm so excited about the second season.

00:05:22.800 --> 00:05:23.810
- Thank you!
- So excited.

00:05:23.810 --> 00:05:25.753
So she really helped you
through everything right?

00:05:25.753 --> 00:05:27.147
- Yeah.
(audience applauds)

00:05:27.147 --> 00:05:30.072
- Zosia, yes, thank you.
(audience cheers)

00:05:30.072 --> 00:05:32.230
Zosia is my co-star and my best friend.

00:05:32.230 --> 00:05:35.100
And she helped me so
much through season two.

00:05:35.100 --> 00:05:38.300
She basically lived with me the
last few months of shooting.

00:05:38.300 --> 00:05:40.263
We just moved in together and she,

00:05:40.263 --> 00:05:43.910
I don't think I would've
gotten to work some days

00:05:43.910 --> 00:05:44.810
without her.

00:05:44.810 --> 00:05:45.950
- Oh I have those friends.

00:05:45.950 --> 00:05:47.440
Yeah, I have, yeah.
- Yeah.

00:05:47.440 --> 00:05:49.780
And I didn't, I never thought
I had to depend on anyone

00:05:49.780 --> 00:05:50.650
like that before.

00:05:50.650 --> 00:05:53.610
And I like really depended
on her and she helped me

00:05:53.610 --> 00:05:56.050
through so much and
she would have days off

00:05:56.050 --> 00:05:58.250
and she would like, oh, I'm gonna cry.

00:05:58.250 --> 00:05:59.760
She would like come to work on days

00:05:59.760 --> 00:06:00.790
she didn't have to be there.

00:06:00.790 --> 00:06:02.170
And like come and have lunch with me.

00:06:02.170 --> 00:06:04.520
And I'm like, "You had
your day off today,"

00:06:04.520 --> 00:06:05.520
and she's like, "I'm coming in"

00:06:05.520 --> 00:06:07.370
'cause she heard I was like
having like a rough time

00:06:07.370 --> 00:06:08.750
and she would like sit in my trailer

00:06:08.750 --> 00:06:11.650
and she's there, she's the best.

00:06:11.650 --> 00:06:13.180
I'm very lucky that I had her.

00:06:13.180 --> 00:06:16.090
- Female friendships,
as far as I'm concerned,

00:06:16.090 --> 00:06:18.790
are my most healthy relationships.

00:06:18.790 --> 00:06:19.939
I feel like, other than my family,

00:06:19.939 --> 00:06:22.130
and they're so good for us

00:06:22.130 --> 00:06:23.000
because I feel like we connect.

00:06:23.000 --> 00:06:25.330
Like even when I was married,

00:06:25.330 --> 00:06:26.770
I mean you connect in a different way

00:06:26.770 --> 00:06:27.640
than you do with your girlfriends.

00:06:27.640 --> 00:06:28.590
- Totally different way.

00:06:28.590 --> 00:06:29.630
It's totally different.

00:06:29.630 --> 00:06:30.463
There's nothing like it.

00:06:30.463 --> 00:06:31.296
- It's so good for us.

00:06:31.296 --> 00:06:33.450
- I'm always promoting that
with my other, everyone.

00:06:33.450 --> 00:06:35.500
I'm like, "You need to have
good girlfriends in your life."

00:06:35.500 --> 00:06:36.510
It's so, so, so important.

00:06:36.510 --> 00:06:38.580
- You know what? I don't
even know if I trust a girl

00:06:38.580 --> 00:06:39.700
that doesn't have a girlfriend.

00:06:39.700 --> 00:06:41.010
- That's a little strange.

00:06:41.010 --> 00:06:42.430
You gotta have a good girlfriend.

00:06:42.430 --> 00:06:43.690
That says a lot about you.

00:06:43.690 --> 00:06:44.813
- I know, someone once
told me, they're like,

00:06:44.813 --> 00:06:45.760
" I don't really have girlfriends."

00:06:45.760 --> 00:06:47.382
And I was like, "That's not shocking."

00:06:47.382 --> 00:06:49.824
(audience laughs)

00:06:49.824 --> 00:06:51.205
I was like, "It's not shocking news."

00:06:51.205 --> 00:06:52.070
- It's very clear.

00:06:52.070 --> 00:06:54.260
- And we call each other out,
but we lift each other up.

00:06:54.260 --> 00:06:56.020
It's like a really healthy, uh anyway.

00:06:56.020 --> 00:06:57.013
- I totally agree.

00:06:58.006 --> 00:06:59.440
- Season two of the show
"The Flight Attendant"

00:06:59.440 --> 00:07:01.530
is on HBO Max.

00:07:01.530 --> 00:07:04.260
And joining us now is
Kaley's friend and costar

00:07:04.260 --> 00:07:05.093
in the series.

00:07:05.093 --> 00:07:08.243
Everybody please welcome Zosia Mamet!

00:07:08.243 --> 00:07:13.243
(upbeat music)
(audience applauds)

00:07:27.795 --> 00:07:29.418
You look so cute.

00:07:29.418 --> 00:07:31.144
All your little tattoos.

00:07:31.144 --> 00:07:32.055
- Oh yeah.

00:07:32.055 --> 00:07:33.248
- I didn't even see you with this outfit.

00:07:33.248 --> 00:07:34.820
- I came to say hi but
you were already out here.

00:07:34.820 --> 00:07:35.700
- Oh my gosh.

00:07:35.700 --> 00:07:37.810
- You also both just
made me cry backstage.

00:07:37.810 --> 00:07:39.768
So that was unfair.

00:07:39.768 --> 00:07:41.120
- And your toes, they're
different on each.

00:07:41.120 --> 00:07:42.720
- Oh that was...
- But that was my idea.

00:07:42.720 --> 00:07:43.790
- That was her idea.

00:07:43.790 --> 00:07:45.600
Also love my hands too.

00:07:45.600 --> 00:07:47.830
- [Kelly] Oh, and the very tips!

00:07:47.830 --> 00:07:49.610
- She likes to credit for her work.

00:07:49.610 --> 00:07:51.840
- I can tell she's humble.

00:07:51.840 --> 00:07:52.750
Well Kaley and I were just talking

00:07:52.750 --> 00:07:54.670
about the strength of
having female friendships.

00:07:54.670 --> 00:07:56.320
Have you always found that's
like really good for you

00:07:56.320 --> 00:07:57.902
and healthy for you as well?

00:07:57.902 --> 00:07:58.735
- Kaley will cry.

00:07:58.735 --> 00:08:00.980
- I went...
- We both we're gonna cry.

00:08:00.980 --> 00:08:03.274
Okay, don't ruin our makeup Kaley Cuoco.

00:08:03.274 --> 00:08:04.818
- It looks so good.

00:08:04.818 --> 00:08:05.690
I know. Leave it to me.

00:08:05.690 --> 00:08:08.453
- Yes. I mean, I think, you know,

00:08:09.321 --> 00:08:12.060
everyone has difficulties in their lives

00:08:12.060 --> 00:08:14.420
and like I'm not super
close with my family

00:08:14.420 --> 00:08:16.410
and I've always found chosen family

00:08:16.410 --> 00:08:17.940
to be so exceptionally important.

00:08:17.940 --> 00:08:19.713
And I think as women, like,

00:08:21.702 --> 00:08:23.010
it's tantamount to anything.

00:08:23.010 --> 00:08:25.100
Obviously like
relationships are important,

00:08:25.100 --> 00:08:26.160
romantic relationships,

00:08:26.160 --> 00:08:28.429
but I think female friendship

00:08:28.429 --> 00:08:30.607
it brings it to another level.

00:08:30.607 --> 00:08:31.440
(laughs) You're gonna make me cry.

00:08:31.440 --> 00:08:33.140
- Is that a tattoo as well on your palm?

00:08:33.140 --> 00:08:34.310
- It is a tattoo.

00:08:34.310 --> 00:08:35.524
- She's a wild child.

00:08:35.524 --> 00:08:36.400
If she could she'd tattoo her hair.

00:08:36.400 --> 00:08:38.307
- Are these like, you drink
a lot and you're like,

00:08:38.307 --> 00:08:39.730
"This would be awesome. Get a heart."

00:08:39.730 --> 00:08:41.127
Or is this just like
you're... what is that?

00:08:41.127 --> 00:08:44.192
- You don't even have to get
me drunk is the sad part.

00:08:44.192 --> 00:08:47.477
Literally, if you right now were like,

00:08:47.477 --> 00:08:49.170
"Do you wanna ditch this
and go get a tattoo?"

00:08:49.170 --> 00:08:50.290
I'd be like, "Sure, let's go.

00:08:50.290 --> 00:08:51.870
- No, because I'm
addicted to them as well.

00:08:51.870 --> 00:08:52.900
I have like 20.
- Oh yeah.

00:08:52.900 --> 00:08:55.293
- Like I have so many, but
they're all little small ones

00:08:55.293 --> 00:08:56.126
- Me too.

00:08:56.126 --> 00:08:56.959
Yeah, so that's why I was wondering

00:08:56.959 --> 00:08:58.747
'cause a couple of mine were like,

00:08:58.747 --> 00:08:59.580
"That sounds like our great idea!"

00:08:59.580 --> 00:09:00.883
- Yes.
- Yeah, yeah.

00:09:01.901 --> 00:09:04.050
- I'm really happy that I haven't made any

00:09:04.050 --> 00:09:06.130
like horrendous decisions.
- Me too.

00:09:06.130 --> 00:09:07.350
Way to go, nicely done.

00:09:07.350 --> 00:09:08.630
- Way to go.

00:09:08.630 --> 00:09:09.570
- Yeah, with a lot of tattoos. It's nice.

00:09:09.570 --> 00:09:10.810
- My husband drunkenly almost got

00:09:10.810 --> 00:09:12.842
a pigeon tattooed on himself.

00:09:12.842 --> 00:09:14.030
And I was like...

00:09:14.030 --> 00:09:17.105
- The rats of the sky.
- Yeah, there you go.

00:09:17.105 --> 00:09:19.022
I don't think I ever told you that.

00:09:19.022 --> 00:09:19.855
- The rats of the sky. (laughs)

00:09:19.855 --> 00:09:20.688
- Right on your body, that's amazing.

00:09:20.688 --> 00:09:21.560
That's cool.

00:09:21.560 --> 00:09:23.000
That's awesome.

00:09:23.000 --> 00:09:25.380
So the show is now in season two,

00:09:25.380 --> 00:09:28.520
is there like a multiple
personality thing going on?

00:09:28.520 --> 00:09:29.353
Is that what's happening?

00:09:29.353 --> 00:09:30.760
- One would think.

00:09:30.760 --> 00:09:32.950
I play five Cassies this season.

00:09:32.950 --> 00:09:34.522
- Is that fun?

00:09:34.522 --> 00:09:37.000
That seems fun. It's not boring at all.

00:09:37.000 --> 00:09:38.330
- [Kaley] It's not boring,

00:09:38.330 --> 00:09:40.200
but it's a lot of working with me.

00:09:40.200 --> 00:09:41.550
So I'd like to maybe...

00:09:41.550 --> 00:09:43.980
- [Kelly] I know, that's
a narcissist run wild.

00:09:43.980 --> 00:09:45.492
- Yes it is!

00:09:45.492 --> 00:09:46.325
- This is what Kaley,

00:09:46.325 --> 00:09:47.480
Kaley comes comes home from a day

00:09:47.480 --> 00:09:49.706
of her working with
herself and she's like...

00:09:49.706 --> 00:09:51.440
(Kaley snort laughs)

00:09:51.440 --> 00:09:54.475
- I'm like, "You would not
believe how I acted today."

00:09:54.475 --> 00:09:56.440
- I work with the biggest diva you know.

00:09:56.440 --> 00:09:57.780
- I'm like, "You wouldn't believe

00:09:57.780 --> 00:09:59.096
what went on with me today."

00:09:59.096 --> 00:10:00.160
- But that had to be a little fun though

00:10:00.160 --> 00:10:01.470
'cause you're not playing
the same character.

00:10:01.470 --> 00:10:02.380
It's not monotonous.

00:10:02.380 --> 00:10:03.460
- It was incredible.

00:10:03.460 --> 00:10:05.560
It was also unbelievably hard work.

00:10:05.560 --> 00:10:06.790
It was very technical.

00:10:06.790 --> 00:10:09.330
Our team actually worked with
the team behind "Orphan Black"

00:10:09.330 --> 00:10:10.410
if you guys know that show.

00:10:10.410 --> 00:10:12.960
They did the same thing that we did.

00:10:12.960 --> 00:10:14.740
It just was very technical.

00:10:14.740 --> 00:10:16.950
A few days I would actually
play five different Cassies.

00:10:16.950 --> 00:10:18.600
So I was like running back and changing.

00:10:18.600 --> 00:10:20.090
And then I was like,
"What personality am I??

00:10:20.090 --> 00:10:23.172
And it was great as an actor.
- That's what I mean!

00:10:23.172 --> 00:10:25.300
- I got to flex a million muscles,

00:10:25.300 --> 00:10:27.510
but yeah, it was a lot and it looks,

00:10:27.510 --> 00:10:29.880
it was so hard to do,
but then watching it back

00:10:29.880 --> 00:10:31.688
I see that it was totally worth it.

00:10:31.688 --> 00:10:33.310
We definitely went big.

00:10:33.310 --> 00:10:34.150
- It looks insane.

00:10:34.150 --> 00:10:36.480
Also just to like brag
about her for a second.

00:10:36.480 --> 00:10:37.360
- Don't brag about me.

00:10:37.360 --> 00:10:38.661
- I'm going to brag about you.

00:10:38.661 --> 00:10:40.560
- No, no, no, don't do it.

00:10:40.560 --> 00:10:43.210
- I know because I was either there

00:10:43.210 --> 00:10:45.511
or she would come home
and crying about it,

00:10:45.511 --> 00:10:47.153
yeah and cry about it,

00:10:47.153 --> 00:10:50.030
how insanely hard it was,

00:10:50.030 --> 00:10:51.490
not only from a technical standpoint,

00:10:51.490 --> 00:10:52.660
but from an acting standpoint,

00:10:52.660 --> 00:10:53.930
what she was going through personally,

00:10:53.930 --> 00:10:56.870
just the whole, this
shoot like was definitely

00:10:56.870 --> 00:10:59.135
blood, sweat and tears for all of us.

00:10:59.135 --> 00:11:02.030
And the first time I saw

00:11:02.030 --> 00:11:03.810
one of the motion capture scenes,

00:11:03.810 --> 00:11:05.690
which is her in gold dress Cassie

00:11:05.690 --> 00:11:08.550
there was, and I was sitting
next to her on her couch

00:11:08.550 --> 00:11:09.970
watching a producer's cut.

00:11:09.970 --> 00:11:12.660
And I was like, "Is that
a different actress?"

00:11:12.660 --> 00:11:16.572
Like she is so mind blowing,
playing these different parts.

00:11:16.572 --> 00:11:17.405
- [Kelly] I love that.

00:11:17.405 --> 00:11:18.400
- It's like she actually am,

00:11:18.400 --> 00:11:19.900
she is a different human being

00:11:19.900 --> 00:11:24.181
and it is five of her
and it is next level.

00:11:24.181 --> 00:11:25.731
- [Kelly] I'm like, so excited.

